{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX031\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers board approval and prior structure authorization/disclosure, but says shareholder approval or prospectus disclosure; the rubric requires both.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Explicitly says the principal adviser oversees sub-advisers and retains overall responsibility.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that an increase in the adviser's fee still requires a shareholder vote.\"},{\"point\":4,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that shareholders receive notice within about 90 days.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"“Shareholders approved the structure, or the initial prospectus disclosed it before public sale.” The rubric requires shareholder approval of the structure initially and prospectus disclosure, not either one alone.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers the board-approval mechanism, ongoing adviser responsibility, fee-vote condition, and optional notice. Its disjunctive statement of the initial authorization and disclosure conditions is a material local error, capping the grade at partial.\"}"}}
